<%# One phase meter inside a repo lane, drawn as a CLICKABLE CARD: a label, then one TALL
    bar that carries the phase's own content INSIDE it — a mark per CI check for Assembling
    (✓ passed · ✗ failed · a spinner while running), or the status word for the coarse and
    deploy phases ("deploying", "live ✓", "n/a"). One bar instead of a bar plus a separate
    fraction chip and check row: same information, half the vertical space. Where the phase
    has a GitHub Actions run, the WHOLE card is the link to it (the ↗ surfaces on hover) —
    click the phase, land on the action in progress.

    Two things here are load-bearing, both learned from reviews that MEASURED them, and
    both guarded by e2e/release_meter_fit.spec.js (the only tier that can see either):

    · FIT. This bar is not a fixed width and does not track the viewport: the lane grid
      sits inside the dashboard's `xl:grid-cols-2`, so the bar measures 174px at a 1024px
      viewport and 80px at 1280px. Eight marks need 78px. So the marks are capped
      (ApplicationHelper::RELEASE_METER_MARK_CAP), each is a fixed 8px shrink-0 box, and
      the bar asks its OWN width (`@container`) — under 99px it drops the marks and shows
      the fraction instead. A cap alone cannot do this, and believing it could is what
      shipped a silent clip: `overflow-hidden` ate the 8th mark with no error, and the
      suite sitting exactly AT the cap draws no overflow "…" to hint at it.
    · CONTRAST. The fill is a TINT, not a block of colour — 15% light, 30% dark — because
      the marks ride on top of it. Same-hue marks on a heavier fill measured 1.73:1. The
      pairs release_meter_tone draws here measure 5.3:1 or better in both themes; the spec
      re-measures the four states the seed RENDERS (see release_meter_tone for the two it
      cannot reach).

    Change either and re-measure; do not re-reason. The spec goes red on a mutation of
    either mechanism — that was checked, not assumed.

    Locals: phase (a release_repo_lanes phase hash). %>
<% phase = local_assigns.fetch(:phase) %>
<% tone = release_meter_tone(phase) %>
<% na = phase[:state].to_sym == :na %>
<% live = phase[:state].to_sym == :running %>
<% ci = phase[:checks] %>
<% marks = release_meter_check_marks(ci) %>
<% overflowed = marks.last == :overflow %>
<% marks = marks.take(marks.size - 1) if overflowed %>
<% linked = phase[:url].present? %>
<%# The card's accessible name. A link takes its name from its subtree, so glyph marks
    alone would announce as noise and the hover title would be DISCARDED — spell the
    summary out here and hide the marks from the a11y tree. %>
<% summary = ci.present? ? "#{ci.passed} of #{ci.total} checks passed" : phase[:value] %>
<% card_title = "#{phase[:label]} — #{phase[:value]}#{". Open the GitHub Actions run." if linked}" %>
<%# The card: an <a> when the phase has a run to open, a plain <div> otherwise — never a
    dead link. -m-1/p-1 keeps the hover surface generous without shifting the grid. %>
<% card_classes = ["group block min-w-0 -m-1 rounded-md p-1 transition-colors"] %>
<% card_classes << "hover:bg-inset/70 focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-primary" if linked %>
<% card_options = { class: card_classes.join(" "), title: card_title, aria: { label: "#{phase[:label]} — #{summary}" } } %>
<% if linked %>
  <% card_options.merge!(href: phase[:url], target: "_blank", rel: "noopener", data: { test: "release-phase-link" }) %>
<% else %>
  <%# A bare <div> would drop its aria-label on the floor; role=img makes the name count. %>
  <% card_options[:role] = "img" %>
<% end %>
<%# data-signature is the live-fx diff (ApplicationHelper#release_meter_signature): the Next
    Release card is REPLACED wholesale on every CI upsert, so LiveBoardFx compares these
    strings across the swap and glows only the meter that moved. It is the GLOW HOST too —
    .studio-team-glow rides this wrapper, which is why the ring is not clipped (the bar
    below is overflow-hidden; its own ::before would be eaten). %>
<div class="min-w-0" data-test="release-phase-meter" data-phase="<%= phase[:key] %>" data-state="<%= phase[:state] %>"
     data-signature="<%= release_meter_signature(phase) %>">
  <%= content_tag(linked ? "a" : "div", card_options) do %>
    <div class="mb-1 flex items-center justify-between gap-1">
      <span class="truncate text-[9px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wide <%= tone[:label] %>"><%= phase[:label] %></span>
      <% if linked %>
        <span aria-hidden="true" class="shrink-0 text-[8px] leading-none opacity-0 transition-opacity group-hover:opacity-100 <%= tone[:label] %>">↗</span>
      <% end %>
    </div>
    <%# @container, not a media query: the meter's width is set by the lane grid INSIDE the
        dashboard grid, so it does not track the viewport — crossing `xl` actually SHRINKS
        it (measured: 174px bar at 1024px wide, 80px at 1280px). The marks show only when
        this bar is genuinely wide enough for them. %>
    <%# The live-fx glow HOST — a bare wrapper the exact size of the bar, so the ring travels
        the BAR's border rather than boxing the label in with it. It cannot be the bar itself
        (overflow-hidden, which clips the check marks, would eat the ring) and it cannot be
        the meter wrapper (that draws a box around the label too — measured, and it read as a
        blob). The ring's ::before sits at z-index -1, so the bar's own opaque fill covers the
        interior and only the 2px margin shows: a border ring, not a wash. %>
    <div class="rounded" data-test="release-phase-glow-host">
    <div class="@container relative h-[18px] overflow-hidden rounded border <%= na ? "border-dashed border-subtle bg-inset/40" : "border-subtle bg-inset" %>"
         data-test="release-phase-bar">
      <% unless na %>
        <%# data-test doubles as the live-fx handle: the glow reads this element's COMPUTED
            background-color for --studio-team-glow-color, so the ring is always the meter's
            own tone (mint done / amber running / red failed) with no second colour table to
            drift from release_meter_tone. %>
        <div class="absolute inset-y-0 left-0 <%= tone[:fill] %> <%= phase[:coarse] && live ? "release-meter-indeterminate opacity-60" : "opacity-15 dark:opacity-30" %>"
             style="width: <%= release_meter_width(phase) %>%" data-test="release-phase-fill"></div>
      <% end %>
      <div class="relative flex h-full min-w-0 items-center gap-[2px] px-1 <%= marks.any? ? "justify-start @max-[99px]:justify-center" : "justify-center" %> <%= tone[:value] %>">
        <% if marks.any? %>
          <%# Decorative: the card's aria-label already says "5 of 8 checks passed", and a
              per-glyph title= would shadow the card's own tooltip on the biggest target. %>
          <span class="flex min-w-0 items-center gap-[2px] overflow-hidden text-[9px] leading-none @max-[99px]:hidden"
                data-test="release-phase-checks" aria-hidden="true">
            <% marks.each do |mark| %>
              <% if mark == :pending %>
                <%# stroke-width 3 (the house loader's 2.5 would land under a pixel at this
                    size: 2.5/24 × 8px ≈ 0.8px). %>
                <svg class="h-2 w-2 shrink-0 animate-spin motion-reduce:animate-none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"
                     data-test="release-check-spinner">
                  <circle class="opacity-25" cx="12" cy="12" r="9" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3"/>
                  <path class="opacity-90" d="M12 3a9 9 0 0 1 9 9" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round"/>
                </svg>
              <% else %>
                <%# Fixed 8px box, same as the spinner: the row's width is then arithmetic,
                    not a bet on how wide the fallback font draws ✓. %>
                <span class="inline-flex h-2 w-2 shrink-0 items-center justify-center leading-none"><%= mark == :failed ? "✗" : "✓" %></span>
              <% end %>
            <% end %>
          </span>
          <% if overflowed %>
            <%# Outside the clipping row on purpose — this glyph must survive. %>
            <span class="shrink-0 text-[9px] leading-none @max-[99px]:hidden" data-test="release-phase-overflow" aria-hidden="true">…</span>
          <% end %>
          <%# Narrow bar: 8 marks need 78px and this bar has less, so the marks would clip
              SILENTLY (a suite sitting exactly at the cap draws no overflow glyph). Below
              99px (the compiled query is `not (min-width:99px)`) the bar shows the fraction
              instead — the same count, in 28px. %>
          <span class="hidden truncate text-[9px] font-bold tabular-nums @max-[99px]:inline"
                data-test="release-phase-compact-value" aria-hidden="true"><%= phase[:value] %></span>
        <% else %>
          <%# No per-check marks (the deploy/coarse/n-a phases): the bar carries the status
              word itself, so the header stays a bare label. %>
          <% if live %><span class="inline-block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 animate-pulse rounded-full bg-current"></span><% end %>
          <span class="truncate text-[9px] font-bold tabular-nums" data-test="release-phase-value" aria-hidden="true"><%= phase[:value] %></span>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    </div>
    </div><%# /release-phase-glow-host %>
  <% end %>
</div>
